{"id": "EUVD-2026-107250", "enisaUuid": "59561813-5d66-37a8-aec6-865abe370d1d", "description": "PHPOffice PHPPresentation through 1.2.0 contains an insecure deserialization vulnerability that allows attackers to instantiate arbitrary PHP objects by supplying a crafted presentation file. Attackers can upload a ZIP containing PhpPresentation.xml that IOFactory::load passes to unserialize(), enabling gadget-chain code execution, file writes, or denial of service.", "datePublished": "2026-10-21T12:39:55", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:39:55", "baseScore": 9.2, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@leediay/multiple_vulnerable_phppresentation", "https://github.com/PHPOffice/PHPPresentation/blob/1.2.0/src/PhpPresentation/Reader/Serialized.php#L77-L109", "https://github.com/PHPOffice/PHPPresentation/blob/1.2.0/src/PhpPresentation/IOFactory.php#L39", "https://github.com/PHPOffice/PHPPresentation", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/phpoffice-phppresentation-through-1.2.0-deserialization-via-reader-serialized-load"], "aliases": ["GHSA-q73p-x2mp-8gm9", "CVE-2026-114403"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.48, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "6a21b180-1d49-32ba-9852-fc18c6714bde", "product": {"name": "PHPPresentation", "vendor": {"name": "PHPOffice"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22641.2.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "3c8f4fac-1ec5-34d0-b7fd-7a644e084264", "vendor": {"name": "PHPOffice"}}], "isExploited": false}